          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "Working with Fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.177,
            0.252,
            0.195
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 176"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.206,
            0.299,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": "？ **Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.229,
            0.847,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "**1. Tenzin drinks** $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ **glass of milk every day. How many glasses of milk does he drink in a week? How many glasses of milk did he drink in the month of January?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.299,
            0.718,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Quantity of milk that Tenzin drinks in a week $= { \\frac { 7 } { 2 } }$ glasses."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.328,
            0.832,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": "Quantity of milk Tenzin drinks in the month of January which has 31 d $\\mathrm { a y s } = { \\frac { 3 1 } { 2 } }$ glasses."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.389,
            0.882,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "**2. A team of workers can make 1 km of a water canal in 8 days. So, in one day, the team can make \\_\\_\\_ km of the water canal. If they work 5 days a week, they can make \\_\\_\\_ km of the water canal in a week.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.448,
            0.169,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.467,
            0.602,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "Length of water canal made in 1 da $\\mathrm { y } = { \\frac { 1 } { 8 } }$ km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.498,
            0.603,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "5 Length of water canal made in 5 days = km. 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.537,
            0.883,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "**3. Manju and two of her neighbours buy 5 litres of oil every week and share it equally among the 3 families. How much oil does each family get in a week? How much oil will one family get in 4 weeks?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.597,
            0.169,
            0.613
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.615,
            0.548,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "Oil each family gets in 1 week $= { \\frac { 5 } { 3 } }$ litres."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.647,
            0.566,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": "Oil each family gets in 4 weeks $\\scriptstyle { \\frac { 2 0 } { 3 } } { \\mathrm { l i t r e s } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.686,
            0.883,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "**4. Safia saw the Moon setting on Monday at 10 pm. Her mother, who is a scientist, told her that every day the Moon sets** $\\frac{5}{6}$ **hour later than the previous day. How many hours after 10 pm will the moon set on Thursday?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.775,
            0.168,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.794,
            0.82,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": "Time at which the moon sets on Thursday (i.e. 3 days after Monday) $10 + 2 + \\frac{1}{2} = 12\\frac{1}{2}$ am Or 12:30 am"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
